<article class="env-definition" id="00NW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00NW">Definition <span data-tag="00NW">10.78.1</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring and $M$ an $R$-module. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say that $M$ is <em>locally free</em> if we can cover $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ by standard opens $D(f_ i)$, $i \in I$ such that $M_{f_ i}$ is a free $R_{f_ i}$-module for all $i \in I$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say that $M$ is <em>finite locally free</em> if we can choose the covering such that each $M_{f_ i}$ is finite free. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say that $M$ is <em>finite locally free of rank $r$</em> if we can choose the covering such that each $M_{f_ i}$ is isomorphic to $R_{f_ i}^{\oplus r}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>